## Context
The OpenRouter worker processes multiple jobs concurrently via the
OpenRouter API, with rate limiting and budget controls.

## Actions
1. Subclass Worker -> OpenRouterWorker in worker.py
2. Parallel execution with configurable concurrency
3. Rate limiting to respect OpenRouter API limits
4. Per-job and global budget tracking via BudgetTracker
5. CLI: `python -m aedist.worker openrouter --concurrency 8`

## Exit criteria
- OpenRouterWorker processes jobs in parallel up to concurrency limit
- Rate limiting prevents API throttling
- Budget exceeded stops all workers gracefully
- CLI entry point works
